# Secrets — never commit keys
.env

# Everything about the person using this app: their profile, their contact
# details, their jobs, their drafts, their cost ledger and their event log.
# Personal data — never tracked, never touched by an update. The one folder to
# copy when moving machines.
#
# Anchored, for the reason spelled out below /profile/: unanchored `data/` would
# also ignore a `data/` directory anywhere else in the tree, and the day somebody
# adds one, its contents go missing from the commit without a word.
/data/
/backups/

# The single-person layout this app used to have. Kept ignored so an older clone
# that still has one does not accidentally commit it after pulling.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose: `profile/` alone matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed server/profile/ — and
# because gitignore does not untrack files that are already tracked, the only
# casualty was the one file in there that was new. It was found by cloning the
# repo and running it, which is the only way that class of mistake ever is.
/profile/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Tooling installed alongside the project rather than part of it: the Claude
# Code skill directory and its local config. Both are regenerated by whoever
# has the tool installed, and neither is this app.
.claude/
.impeccable/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Exported PDFs anywhere in the tree — application materials are personal data
*.pdf
